# DiamaneOS: the VM manager runs under a seccomp filter (packages/modules/Virtualization
# android/virtmgr/src/seccomp.rs), which needs no_new_privs. With no_new_privs a process changes domain on exec only
# where process2 nnp_transition is allowed, so without this rule no VM manager could start its crosvm. It grants no
# domain change: each client's VM manager may still only change to its own crosvm domain (virtualizationmanager_domain
# in te_macros). It only keeps no_new_privs from blocking those changes.
allow virtualizationmanager_domain crosvm_domain:process2 nnp_transition;
